{%- comment -%}
  PG Nav: bigger header links.

  pg-mobile sets the nav in Press Start 2P at 11px (9px under 760px), which it
  chose because that face runs very wide -- it was sized down from the Roboto
  Slab it replaced. It ended up smaller than the rest of the header reads.

  11px -> 14px, and 9px -> 11px on phones. Press Start 2P is drawn on an 8px
  grid, so the sizes stay whole pixels rather than fractional ones that get
  resampled and blur.

  The gaps come in slightly (54px -> 46px, 22px -> 18px) to pay for the extra
  glyph width, so "TRACK YOUR ORDER" and "CONTACT" still sit on one line at the
  narrow widths. word-spacing stays as pg-mobile set it: the face draws a
  full-cell space, so without it a multi-word link reads as separate links.

  Same specificity as pg-mobile's rule and this section loads after it, so it
  wins on source order.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
/* ---------------- header row height ----------------
   pg-mobile gives the logo box `min-height:252px`, sized for the wordmark at
   its old 2.6 vertical scale. The mark is now 15% shorter and 10% smaller, so
   it draws about 178px tall at the widest breakpoint and that 252px is mostly
   empty space above and below it. The box comes down to 190px, which still
   clears the mark -- it is drawn with a transform, so it can overflow its line
   box and the header clips at overflow:hidden.

   Phones get proportionally tighter boxes, and the header/nav padding comes in
   with them, so the whole bar under the announcement carousel is shorter. */
html body .pgh-logo,
html body .pgx-logo,
html body .pgc-logo{min-height:190px !important}
html body .pgh-head-in,
html body .pgx-head-in,
html body .pgc-head-in{padding-top:10px !important;padding-bottom:4px !important}
html body .pgh-nav,
html body .pgx-nav,
html body .pgc-nav{padding-top:4px !important;padding-bottom:12px !important}

@media (max-width:760px){
  html body .pgh-logo,
  html body .pgx-logo,
  html body .pgc-logo{min-height:140px !important}
}
@media (max-width:560px){
  html body .pgh-logo,
  html body .pgx-logo,
  html body .pgc-logo{min-height:104px !important}
  html body .pgh-head-in,
  html body .pgx-head-in,
  html body .pgc-head-in{padding-top:8px !important;padding-bottom:2px !important}
  html body .pgh-nav,
  html body .pgx-nav,
  html body .pgc-nav{padding-top:2px !important;padding-bottom:10px !important}
}

/* ---------------- nav links ---------------- */
html body .pgh-nav a,
html body .pgx-nav a,
html body .pgc-nav a,
html body .pgf-nav a{
  font-size:14px !important;
  line-height:1.8 !important;
}
html body .pgh-nav,
html body .pgx-nav,
html body .pgc-nav,
html body .pgf-nav{gap:46px !important}

@media (max-width:760px){
  html body .pgh-nav a,
  html body .pgx-nav a,
  html body .pgc-nav a,
  html body .pgf-nav a{font-size:11px !important}
  html body .pgh-nav,
  html body .pgx-nav,
  html body .pgc-nav,
  html body .pgf-nav{gap:18px !important}
}

/* ---------------- nav centring ----------------
   The nav sat off-centre against the page's own centre line -- the section
   headings under it ("MOST LOVED" / "Best Sellers") and the product carousel
   centre on the viewport, and the nav did not line up with them.

   The row is centred within whatever box it is given, so any asymmetry comes
   from that box rather than from the links: a nav that is not full width, or
   that inherits one-sided padding or margin from the header layout, centres
   its links around its own middle instead of the page's. Pinning the row to
   the full width with symmetric edges puts its centre back on the page's.

   flex-wrap stays on so "TRACK YOUR ORDER" can drop to its own line on a
   narrow phone rather than overflowing, and the wrapped rows stay centred. */
html body .pgh-nav,
html body .pgx-nav,
html body .pgc-nav,
html body .pgf-nav{
  display:flex !important;
  flex-wrap:wrap !important;
  justify-content:center !important;
  align-items:center !important;
  text-align:center !important;
  width:100% !important;
  max-width:100% !important;
  box-sizing:border-box !important;
  margin-left:auto !important;
  margin-right:auto !important;
  padding-left:16px !important;
  padding-right:16px !important;
  float:none !important;
}
</style>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Nav", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
